(let [template (load-file "public/chp/template.chp")]
  (clojure.walk/postwalk-replace
    {:template/title "Datom.World: Sovereign Computing with Immutable Tuples & Continuous Streams"
     :template/content
     (list
       [:section.hero
        [:div.section-inner
         [:div.hero-grid
          [:div.hero-copy
           [:div.hero-badge
            [:span.hero-badge-dot]
            [:span "Beyond the Client-Server Web"]]
           [:h1 "Share data without losing control."]
           [:p.lead
            "Computation should move freely, but state must remain sovereign. "
            "Datom.World is an open architecture built on mobile continuations running inside sandboxed Yin.VMs, "
            "where immutable fact-streams carry context wherever work travels next."]
           [:div.hero-actions
            [:a.btn.btn-primary {:href "/demo.html"} "Explore the Live Demo"]
            [:a.btn.btn-secondary {:href "#axioms"} "Read the 4 Axioms"]]]
          [:div.hero-specimen
           [:div.specimen-header
            [:span.specimen-tag "Canonical Primitive"]
            [:span.specimen-meta "Moduli Dimension: d5"]]
           [:div.tuple-display
            [:div.tuple-bracket "["]
            [:div.tuple-item
             [:span.tuple-sym "e"]
             [:span.tuple-name "entity"]
             [:span.tuple-sub "identity"]]
            [:div.tuple-item
             [:span.tuple-sym "a"]
             [:span.tuple-name "attribute"]
             [:span.tuple-sub "dimension"]]
            [:div.tuple-item
             [:span.tuple-sym "v"]
             [:span.tuple-name "value"]
             [:span.tuple-sub "payload"]]
            [:div.tuple-item
             [:span.tuple-sym "t"]
             [:span.tuple-name "time/tx"]
             [:span.tuple-sub "causality"]]
            [:div.tuple-item
             [:span.tuple-sym "m"]
             [:span.tuple-name "meta"]
             [:span.tuple-sub "provenance"]]
            [:div.tuple-bracket "]"]]
           [:p.specimen-caption "Every message, file, database record, and execution trace collapses into an append-only datom stream."]]]]]

       [:section.section-dark
        [:div.section-inner
         [:div.section-header-block
          [:span.section-kicker "Shared Intelligence"]
          [:h2 "Durable Memory for Autonomous Agents"]]
         [:div.text-columns-2
          [:div
           [:p.prose-text
            "For modern AI agents, context lost is reasoning destroyed. Short-term prompts, ephemeral scratchpads, and opaque cache vectors fail when multi-agent swarms attempt rigorous long-horizon coordination. "
            "In Datom.World, memory is never trapped inside an ephemeral inference session."]
           [:p.prose-text
            "Every state transition, belief update, and execution trace is materialized as an immutable datom in an append-only stream. "
            "Agents reason over time-traveling Datalog facts with mathematical certainty, eliminating accidental context clobbering."]]
          [:div
           [:p.prose-text
            "Through " [:strong "DaoSpace"] ", multiple sovereign agents coordinate stigmergically over a shared environment of immutable tuples. "
            "Rather than fragile RPC handoffs, agents deposit facts and observe stream transformations—mirroring biological swarm intelligence."]
           [:div.callout-link-box
            [:span "In-depth research:"]
            [:a {:href "/blog/containing-agent-smith.blog"} "Containing Agent Smith in a Pocket Universe"]
            [:a {:href "/blog/agent-smith-hippocampus.blog"} "Agent Smith as the Hippocampus"]]]]]]

       [:section.section-light
        [:div.section-inner
         [:div.section-header-block
          [:span.section-kicker "Foundational Principles"]
          [:h2 {:id "axioms"} "The Four Axioms"]
          [:p.section-subtitle "Datom.World discards accidental software complexity in favor of four immutable principles."]]
         [:div.axioms-flow
          [:article.axiom-row
           [:div.axiom-num "01"]
           [:div.axiom-body
            [:h3 "Everything is a Stream"]
            [:p "Streams transport whatever values each computational layer requires. Persistent facts are datoms: immutable tuples formatted as " [:code "[e a v t m]"] ". Transaction IDs are strictly monotonic within each stream; cross-stream causality is preserved via metadata."]
            [:p "Benefits: Complete provenance, time-travel queries across historical states, and a unified substrate where messages, files, and state changes collapse into the same primitive."]
            [:div.axiom-links
             [:span "Read:"]
             [:a {:href "/blog/datoms-as-streams.blog"} "Streaming Datoms with Transducers"]
             [:a {:href "/blog/ast-higher-dimensional-datom-streams.blog"} "AST as Higher Dimensional Streams"]
             [:a {:href "/blog/daospace-distributed-database-immutable-streams.blog"} "DaoSpace on Immutable Streams"]]]]

          [:article.axiom-row
           [:div.axiom-num "02"]
           [:div.axiom-body
            [:h3 "Interpretation Creates Semantics"]
            [:p "Data in isolation is pure syntax. Semantics emerge only when an interpreter observes and evaluates it. This is the " [:strong "One Truth, Many Perspectives"] " principle: a single immutable stream of datoms can be projected into a 3D visual scene, a relational table, or a state machine without mutating the underlying truth."]
            [:p "New interpreters never break existing models, enabling backward-compatible evolution and synthetic agents that learn and re-interpret history freely."]
            [:div.axiom-links
             [:span "Read:"]
             [:a {:href "/blog/structure-vs-interpretation.blog"} "Structure vs Interpretation"]
             [:a {:href "/blog/semantics-structure-interpretation.blog"} "Semantics as Structure Through Observers"]
             [:a {:href "/blog/datom-world-wave-function-collapse.blog"} "Datom.World & Wave Function Collapse"]]]]

          [:article.axiom-row
           [:div.axiom-num "03"]
           [:div.axiom-body
            [:h3 "Code and State are Datoms"]
            [:p "Because code and runtime state are both datoms, the " [:strong "Universal Abstract Syntax Tree (AST)"] " is the canonical program representation. Code text is merely one projection of this AST. Like ideographic characters providing a semantic bridge across dialects, Universal AST enables loss-less cross-language translation (Python to C++) and structural editing without parse errors."]
            [:div.axiom-links
             [:span "Read:"]
             [:a {:href "/blog/yin-vm-ast-chinese-characters.blog"} "Yin.vm: Universal Ideographs for Code"]
             [:a {:href "/blog/ide-edits-ast-not-text.blog"} "When the IDE Edits AST, Not Text"]
             [:a {:href "/blog/universal-ast-vs-assembly.blog"} "Universal AST vs Assembly"]]]]

          [:article.axiom-row
           [:div.axiom-num "04"]
           [:div.axiom-body
            [:h3 "Everything is a Continuation"]
            [:p "If streams are how data flows, continuations are how computation flows. Every executing process in the Yin VM is a " [:strong "first-class continuation"] "—a serializable snapshot that can pause, travel across physical networks, and resume with state intact."]
            [:p "Enables code mobility: start execution on a mobile device, offload compute to a high-density GPU cluster, and return results without losing thread context."]
            [:div.axiom-links
             [:span "Read:"]
             [:a {:href "/blog/computation-moves-data-stays.blog"} "Computation Moves, Data Stays"]
             [:a {:href "/blog/continuations-universal-semantic-kernel.blog"} "Continuations as the Universal Kernel"]
             [:a {:href "/blog/why-udp-not-tcp.blog"} "Why TCP is Too Semantic"]]]]]]]

       [:section.section-dark
        [:div.section-inner
         [:div.section-header-block
          [:span.section-kicker "Architectural Shift"]
          [:h2 "Recomposing the Web Stack"]
          [:p.section-subtitle "How legacy client-server mechanisms transform into sovereign stream primitives."]]
         [:div.table-container
          [:table.recomposition-table
           [:thead
            [:tr
             [:th "Legacy Web Paradigm"]
             [:th "Datom.World Primitive"]
             [:th "Structural Shift"]]]
           [:tbody
            [:tr
             [:td [:strong "JavaScript VM"] [:br] [:span.dim "Imperative runtime on remote host"]]
             [:td [:strong "Yin VM"] [:br] [:a {:href "/yin.chp"} "Continuation Engine"]]
             [:td "Computation is serializable, pauseable, and travels across sovereign machines."]]
            [:tr
             [:td [:strong "HTTP Request / Response"] [:br] [:span.dim "Stateless client-server fetch"]]
             [:td [:strong "DaoStream"] [:br] [:a {:href "/dao-stream.chp"} "Causal Stream Transport"]]
             [:td "Data streams continuously between entangled nodes through append-only facts."]]
            [:tr
             [:td [:strong "LocalStorage / SQL RDBMS"] [:br] [:span.dim "Centralized relational tables"]]
             [:td [:strong "DaoSpace + DaoJing"] [:br] [:a {:href "/dao-space.chp"} "Stigmergic Tuple Space"]]
             [:td "Content-addressed immutable storage queried via reactive Datalog expressions."]]
            [:tr
             [:td [:strong "DOM / HTML Layout"] [:br] [:span.dim "Rigid document tree render"]]
             [:td [:strong "PostGraphics"] [:br] [:a {:href "/post-graphics.chp"} "Frame Program Stream"]]
             [:td "Terminals interpret frame data into WebGPU, canvas, or Flutter GPU surfaces."]]]]]
         [:div.quote-panel
          [:p "“Any software—operating system, compiler, database, 3D world, or AI agent—is fundamentally an interpreter of datom streams.”"]]]]

       [:section.section-light
        [:div.section-inner
         [:div.anti-spam-grid
          [:div
           [:span.section-kicker "Economic Sovereignty"]
           [:h2 "Keeping Open Networks Spam-Free"]
           [:p.prose-text
            "Open decentralized protocols face an existential problem: as network utility grows, spam and Sybil traffic overwhelm participants. Traditional platforms react with centralized gatekeeping or black-box moderation algorithms."]
           [:p.prose-text
            "Datom.World deploys " [:strong "Shibi"] ": a capability-based economic layer that makes abusive spam computationally and economically unviable without censorship."]
           [:p.prose-text
            "Nodes mint customized, purpose-specific capabilities. To append to a stream or request compute, callers present valid Shibi tokens. Attention becomes a sovereign, cryptographically secured boundary."]
           [:div.axiom-links
            [:span "Learn more:"]
            [:a {:href "/shibi.chp"} "How Shibi Works"]
            [:a {:href "/blog/shibi-as-money.blog"} "Why Shibi is Capability, Not Money"]]]
          [:div.shibi-specimen
           [:div.shibi-card
            [:div.shibi-header
             [:span.shibi-symbol "§"]
             [:span.shibi-title "Shibi Capability Token"]]
            [:div.shibi-code
             "[:shibi/capability {:issuer \"did:datom:node-8f2\" :scope :stream/append :cost-factor 1.0}]"]
            [:p.shibi-note "Peer authorization without centralized token registries."]]]]]])}
    template))
